IMPORT prelude

-- Plant Varieties Protection Act 2004 (Singapore) -- who may apply (s 2 "breeder"), when a variety is new and the foreign
-- priority claim that moves the novelty date (ss 14, 22), when the Registrar must grant protection (s 21), how long it lasts and how
-- it ends (ss 24 to 27), what it lets the grantee stop and the exceptions (ss 28 to 32), money remedies for infringement (s 30),
-- compulsory licences (s 34), denominations (s 36), offences and composition (ss 10, 11, 44 to 46, 52) and appeals (s 48).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation (version in force from
-- 10 June 2022), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PVPA2004.txt. The latest amendments annotated are Act 7 of 2022 (wef
-- 26 May 2022) and Act 23 of 2019 (wef 10 June 2022, s 52).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0084 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- SCOPED to what a breeder, a nursery, a farmer or a home gardener meets. Not encoded: administration (ss 5 to 9, 12), application
-- procedure and publication (ss 13, 15 to 19), provisional protection (s 20), competing independent breeders (s 23), the
-- transitional novelty rule for genera added in 2014 (s 22(4)), assignment and licences binding successors (s 28(3) to (6)),
-- notice of protection (s 35), use of denominations beyond the offence (s 37), the register (ss 39 to 43), and anything in rules
-- (no subsidiary legislation was retrieved: the prescribed periods, fees and the genera exempt under s 31(2) are unknown here).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Plant Varieties Protection Act 2004 -- protection`

§§ `2 -- the breeder`

-- s 2 "breeder": (a) "a person who bred, or discovered and developed, the plant variety"; (b) if bred "in the course of performing the
-- person's duties or functions as an employee of another person, that other person"; or (c) "the successor in title" to (a) or (b).
-- s 13(1): an application "must be made by the breeder".
DECLARE Breeder IS ONE OF
    `the person who bred it`
    `the employer`
    `the successor in title`

GIVEN `bred in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `rights passed to a successor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Breeder
`who is the breeder` MEANS
    IF `rights passed to a successor` THEN `the successor in title`
    ELSE IF `bred in the course of employment` THEN `the employer`
         ELSE `the person who bred it`

§§ `14, 22(1) to (3) -- novelty and the priority claim`

-- s 22(1)(a): new if harvested or propagating material "has not been sold or otherwise disposed of to another person, by or with the
-- breeder's consent for the purposes of exploitation" (i) "earlier than 12 months before the date the application is made" where the
-- sale and exploitation is in Singapore; (ii) "earlier than 6 years before that date in the case of trees or vines, or earlier than
-- 4 years before that date in any other case" where outside Singapore.
-- s 22(2): no account is taken of a sale under an arrangement to increase stock or test, where unused material and its produce
-- return to the breeder. s 22(3): novelty survives sale of (a) material that is neither propagating nor harvested material, or
-- (b) surplus propagating material of the breeding work sold "without variety identification for purposes of consumption".
-- s 14(1): a breeder who applied in another UPOV member and applies here "within 12 months after" the earliest foreign application
-- may claim priority, and "sections 22 and 23 apply ... as if it had been made on the date the foreign application ... was made".
-- Periods are in months (6 years = 72, 4 years = 48). A sale exactly 12 months before is not "earlier than" 12 months, so it is
-- harmless. Mixed cases (sold in Singapore, exploited abroad) are not addressed by the text and not modelled.
DECLARE Sale HAS
    `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months before the Singapore application` IS A NUMBER
    `by or with the breeder's consent for exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under a stock-increase or testing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of material neither propagating nor harvested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of surplus breeding material sold unidentified for consumption` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `claims priority` IS A BOOLEAN, `months after the earliest foreign application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the priority claim is good` IF
    `claims priority` AND `months after the earliest foreign application` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale, `a tree or vine` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims priority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months after the earliest foreign application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months before the effective application date` MEANS
    IF `the priority claim is good` `claims priority` `months after the earliest foreign application`
    THEN `the sale`'s `months before the Singapore application` MINUS `months after the earliest foreign application`
    ELSE `the sale`'s `months before the Singapore application`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale, `a tree or vine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grace period in months` MEANS
    IF `the sale`'s `in Singapore` THEN 12
    ELSE IF `a tree or vine` THEN 72
         ELSE 48

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale, `a tree or vine` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims priority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months after the earliest foreign application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale destroys novelty` IF
        `the sale`'s `by or with the breeder's consent for exploitation`
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `under a stock-increase or testing arrangement`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `of material neither propagating nor harvested`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `of surplus breeding material sold unidentified for consumption`)
    AND `months before the effective application date` `the sale` `a tree or vine` `claims priority` `months after the earliest foreign application`
            GREATER THAN `the grace period in months` `the sale` `a tree or vine`

§§ `21 -- the Registrar must grant`

-- s 21(1): the Registrar "must" (a) except where withdrawn or lapsed under s 19, grant every eligible application and (b) decline
-- every other. (2): eligible "if, and only if" (a) the applicant complied with s 13 and s 17 or 18, and (b) the Registrar (i) approved
-- the denomination, (ii) is satisfied the applicant is the breeder, and (iii) is satisfied the variety is "new, distinct, stable and
-- uniform within the meaning of section 22".
DECLARE Application HAS
    `complied with section 13` IS A BOOLEAN
    `complied with section 17 or 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `denomination approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applicant is the breeder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `new` IS A BOOLEAN
    `distinct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uniform` IS A BOOLEAN
    `withdrawn or lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must grant protection` IF
        (NOT `the application`'s `withdrawn or lapsed`)
    AND `the application`'s `complied with section 13`
    AND `the application`'s `complied with section 17 or 18`
    AND `the application`'s `denomination approved`
    AND `the application`'s `applicant is the breeder`
    AND `the application`'s `new`
    AND `the application`'s `distinct`
    AND `the application`'s `stable`
    AND `the application`'s `uniform`

§§ `24 to 27 -- term, cancellation, invalidity, renunciation`

-- s 24(2): "the term of a grant of protection is a period of 25 calendar years from the date of the grant", subject to ss 25 and 26.
-- (3) an annual fee; (4) a late fee may be imposed by rules. s 26(2): the grant "must be cancelled by the Registrar" if (a) the
-- grantee fails to provide requested material verifying maintenance, (b) "in any particular year" the annual or late fee "has not been
-- paid within the prescribed period", or (c) the grantee fails to propose a new denomination under s 38. s 27: the grantee may
-- renounce in writing. A grant removed from the register (ss 25(3), 26(4), 27(2)) is treated here as no longer in force -- an
-- inference; the text says it must be removed, not when it stops having effect.
GIVEN `years since the grant` IS A NUMBER, `removed from the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is in force` IF
    `years since the grant` LESS THAN 25 AND (NOT `removed from the register`)

GIVEN `failed to verify maintenance when asked` IS A BOOLEAN, `a year's fee unpaid in the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `failed to propose a new denomination when asked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must cancel` IF
        `failed to verify maintenance when asked`
    OR  `a year's fee unpaid in the prescribed period`
    OR  `failed to propose a new denomination when asked`

-- s 25(2): the Court must declare the grant invalid if (a) the variety "is not new or distinct"; (b) "where the grant of protection was
-- made on the basis of an examination report by an Examiner lodged under section 18" (a foreign report), the variety was not stable or
-- uniform at the time of the grant; or (c) the grant was made to a person not entitled to it, "unless it has since been transferred
-- to the person who is so entitled". s 26(3): the Court cancels a grant if the variety "is no longer stable or uniform".
GIVEN `not new or distinct` IS A BOOLEAN, `granted on a foreign examination report` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `not stable or uniform when granted` IS A BOOLEAN, `granted to a person not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `since transferred to the person entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court must declare the grant invalid` IF
        `not new or distinct`
    OR  (`granted on a foreign examination report` AND `not stable or uniform when granted`)
    OR  (`granted to a person not entitled` AND (NOT `since transferred to the person entitled`))

§§ `29 -- essentially derived varieties`

-- s 29(1): the grant "also extends to" (a) a variety essentially derived from the original, (b) a variety "not distinct" from it, and
-- (c) a variety "the production of which requires the repeated use of the original". (2): essentially derived if (a) predominantly
-- derived from the original (or from a variety itself predominantly derived from it); (b) it retains the essential characteristics
-- of the original's genotype; (c) it "is clearly distinguishable from the original"; and (d) apart from the derivation, it conforms
-- to the original in those essential characteristics.
GIVEN `predominantly derived` IS A BOOLEAN, `retains the essential characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `clearly distinguishable` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise conforms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the variety is essentially derived` IF
    `predominantly derived` AND `retains the essential characteristics` AND `clearly distinguishable` AND `otherwise conforms`

GIVEN `essentially derived` IS A BOOLEAN, `clearly distinguishable` IS A BOOLEAN, `needs repeated use of the original` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant extends to the other variety` IF
    `essentially derived` OR (NOT `clearly distinguishable`) OR `needs repeated use of the original`

§§ `28, 30 to 32 -- infringement and its exceptions`

-- s 28(1): the grantee may prevent, without authorisation, these acts in respect of propagating material: (a) production or
-- reproduction; (b) conditioning for propagation; (c) offering for sale; (d) selling or other marketing; (e) export; (f) import;
-- (g) stocking for any of those. (7): the same rights apply to harvested material "obtained through the unauthorised use of
-- propagating material ... unless the grantee has had a reasonable opportunity" to act against that use first.
-- s 30(1): infringed by a person who (a) not entitled, does in Singapore any s 28(1) act on propagating or harvested material;
-- (c) imports without consent harvested material of the protected variety from a non-UPOV country (or a UPOV member where no
-- equivalent protection is possible). "Harvested material" is defined in s 2 by reference to s 28(7); this encoding reads the
-- s 30(1)(c) limb as covering any harvested material, since otherwise it would add nothing to (a) -- an inference.
-- s 31(1): not an infringement to do "(a) any act privately and for a non-commercial purpose; (b) any act for any experimental or
-- research purpose; or (c) any act for the purposes of breeding any other plant variety". (2): farm-saved seed, only for genera
-- "prescribed ... as exempt". s 32(1): an act concerning material "sold or otherwise marketed in Singapore by or with the grantee's
-- consent" does not infringe, "unless such act involves (c) further propagation" or (d) export of propagable material to a country
-- not protecting the genus, "except where the exported material is for final consumption purposes".
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `producing or reproducing`
    `conditioning for propagation`
    `offering for sale`
    `selling or marketing`
    `exporting`
    `importing`
    `stocking for any of those`
    `displaying or consuming`

DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `the act` IS AN Act
    `on propagating material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on harvested material from unauthorised propagation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the grantee had a reasonable opportunity earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imports harvested material from a non-protecting country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by the grantee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `private and non-commercial` IS A BOOLEAN
    `experimental or research` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for breeding another variety` IS A BOOLEAN
    `farm-saved under a prescribed exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `material first sold in Singapore with consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves further propagation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exports propagable material to a non-protecting country, not for consumption` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is listed in section 28(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`'s `the act`
    WHEN `displaying or consuming` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is covered` IF
        `the conduct`'s `on propagating material`
    OR  (`the conduct`'s `on harvested material from unauthorised propagation` AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `the grantee had a reasonable opportunity earlier`))

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception applies` IF
        `the conduct`'s `private and non-commercial`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `experimental or research`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `for breeding another variety`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `farm-saved under a prescribed exemption`
    OR  (    `the conduct`'s `material first sold in Singapore with consent`
         AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `involves further propagation`)
         AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `exports propagable material to a non-protecting country, not for consumption`))

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct infringes` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `authorised by the grantee`)
    AND (NOT `an exception applies` `the conduct`)
    AND (    (    `the act is listed in section 28(1)` `the conduct`
              AND `the material is covered` `the conduct`
              AND `the conduct`'s `done in Singapore`)
         OR  `the conduct`'s `imports harvested material from a non-protecting country`)

-- s 30(2): relief includes an injunction and "either damages or an account of profits". (3) additional damages for flagrancy.
-- (4): where the defendant proves he "was not aware and had no reasonable grounds for supposing that it was an infringement", the
-- claimant "is not entitled ... to any damages" but "is entitled instead to an account of profits". (5) other relief unaffected.
GIVEN `infringement established` IS A BOOLEAN, `defendant proved innocence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages are available` IF
    `infringement established` AND (NOT `defendant proved innocence`)

GIVEN `infringement established` IS A BOOLEAN, `defendant proved innocence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an account of profits is available` IF
    `infringement established`

§§ `34 -- compulsory licences`

-- s 34(2): the Court may order a compulsory licence "if, and only if" satisfied it "is in the public interest"; (5) not to a person
-- unable to show it can exploit the variety "in a manner acceptable to the Court"; (6) not unless the applicant "has first taken all
-- reasonable steps to obtain authorisation from the grantee on reasonable commercial terms" and failed within a reasonable time.
GIVEN `in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `can exploit acceptably` IS A BOOLEAN, `first sought a licence and failed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may grant a compulsory licence` IF
    `in the public interest` AND `can exploit acceptably` AND `first sought a licence and failed`

§§ `36(3) -- denominations the Registrar must refuse`

-- s 36(3): the Registrar "must not approve or register" a denomination which (a) "consists solely of figures, except where this is an
-- established practice"; (b) is likely to mislead or confuse about the variety or the breeder; (c) is contrary to law or public order
-- or offensive; (d) or (e) is likely to cause confusion with another's trade mark or rights (or the applicant's own mark for other
-- material).
GIVEN `figures only` IS A BOOLEAN, `figures are established practice` IS A BOOLEAN, `misleading` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unlawful or offensive` IS A BOOLEAN, `confusable with a trade mark or other right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse the denomination` IF
        (`figures only` AND (NOT `figures are established practice`))
    OR  `misleading`
    OR  `unlawful or offensive`
    OR  `confusable with a trade mark or other right`

§§ `10, 11, 44 to 46, 52 -- offences and composition`

-- s 10(3), 11(2): failing to obey a summons or refusing to give evidence -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or ... imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding 3 months or ... both". s 44: falsifying the register, knowingly -- "$50,000 or ... 5 years or ... both". s 45: falsely
-- representing a variety as protected, knowingly -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000" (no imprisonment). s 46: "wilfully or negligently"
-- contravening s 37(1), (2) or (3) on denominations -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000".
-- s 52(1): an offence PRESCRIBED as compoundable may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount
-- of the maximum fine" and (b) "$5,000". (Which offences are prescribed was not retrieved.)
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `disobeying a summons of the Registrar`
    `refusing to give evidence`
    `falsifying the register`
    `falsely representing a variety as protected`
    `misusing a denomination`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disobeying a summons of the Registrar` THEN 2000
    WHEN `refusing to give evidence` THEN 2000
    WHEN `falsifying the register` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disobeying a summons of the Registrar` THEN 3
    WHEN `refusing to give evidence` THEN 3
    WHEN `falsifying the register` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can collect` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `48 -- appeals`

-- s 48(1): "there is no appeal to the Court from a decision of the Registrar" except under (2) or rules. (2): appealable are decisions
-- (a) to decline to make a grant, (b) to make a grant, (c) "approving or disapproving a proposed denomination". (Appeals provided for
-- by rules were not retrieved.)
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `declining a grant`
    `making a grant`
    `approving or disapproving a denomination`
    `cancelling a grant for an unpaid fee`
    `awarding costs`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act gives an appeal to the Court` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `declining a grant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making a grant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `approving or disapproving a denomination` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
